        "original_id": "8a25eae6-13a4-5d7d-8605-39d3b02f3937",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Events: 2016 North Dakota gubernatorial election, 2016 United States presidential election\n- Places: North Dakota, United States\n- People: Donald Trump, Mike Pence, Hillary Clinton, Tim Kaine\n- Roles: Governor of North Dakota, Lieutenant Governor of North Dakota, U.S. Senator, U.S. Representative, Indiana Governor, Secretary of State, First Lady\n- Topics: concurrent elections\n\nFacts:\n- The 2016 North Dakota gubernatorial election was held on November 8, 2016, to elect the Governor and Lieutenant Governor of North Dakota.\n- The 2016 North Dakota gubernatorial election was held concurrently with the 2016 United States presidential election, elections to the United States Senate, elections to the United States House of Representatives, and various state and local elections.\n- In the 2016 United States presidential election, the Republican ticket of Donald Trump and Mike Pence defeated the Democratic ticket of Hillary Clinton and Tim Kaine in a surprise victory.",
